# What the jre-example form, booted as it ships, without a shell, must say on its
# console (make check-shellfree-jre-example; test/console.zig; forms/demo/test/console
# has the format). Its native tests check that it answers.
# The JDK's web server starts, leashed, and listens.

seen    app-leashed       leash: \{"event":"start","service":"app"
seen    app-listening     Serving /usr/lib/app/www and subdirectories on 0\.0\.0\.0
up  service-down
unseen  app-failed        Error: |Exception in thread
